  "query_preview": "to include areas along and south of the Missouri River \nwhere daytime heat index values will remain between 105-110 each day \nand 75-80 each night. A Heat Advisory remains in effect through \nThursday evening north of the Excessive Heat Warning along the \nHighway 36 corridor. This prolonged heat event will come courtesy of \na upper ridge that resides over much of the southern CONUS into the \ncentral Rockies. This upper level ridge will slowly slide east \nthrough the week with the ridge axis moving over the local area \nThursday. This will keep highs in the 90s to around 100 through \nThursday. The local area will be on the northern periphery of this \nridge, with weak shortwaves rounding the ridge moving into the area \nproviding occasional slight chance to chance PoPs (20-40%) across \nnorthern Missouri though Thursday night. \n\nFriday into Friday night, a relatively stronger shortwave will move \nacross the northern/central Plains into the Upper Midwest. This will \nact to flatten the ridge and force a weak surface boundary into the \nnorthern CWA. This is expected to bring slightly cooler temperatures \nto northern Missouri with highs in the upper 80s to lower 90s. \nHowever, south of this surface boundary temperatures will continue \nto remain hot with highs remaining in the mid 90s to near 100. This \nboundary may also be the focus for slight chance to chance (20-40%) \nconvection Friday into Friday night across the northern CWA. \nContinued shortwaves are expected to help slowly force this boundary \nsouthward through the area through the weekend continuing to keep \nslight chance to chance PoPs around for the weekend. By Sunday, \ntemperature are expected to range from the mid 80s north to the mid \n90s south. Monday, with the upper level ridge remaining flattened \nacross the region a shortwave is expected to move through the area \nbringing another chance for storms which is forecast to aid in cooler \ntemperatures into the lower 80s to lower 90s.",
